Sanguis Bestrum is the blanket term for the symptoms experienced by those who consume the blood of Beast. Commonly known as lycanthropy, most afflicted by beastblood gain bestial characteristics such as fur growth, increased muscle density and size, and suppressed inhibitions and morality responses.
